From de2accd926b398f2f398bc58534acffef5d87476 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChenXiaoSong <chenxiaosong@kylinos.cn>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:08:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] smb/server: create symbolic link reparse points

Implement FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT using the validated target parser and
private xattr format. Accept empty file or directory placeholders while
preserving their inodes and open handles. Reject invalid data, nonempty
objects, public EAs, streams and handles without write access.

Advertise FILE_SUPPORTS_REPARSE_POINTS now that creation is available.
This enables native ln -s on ordinary Linux CIFS mounts as well as POSIX
mounts. Keep data operations blocked on the original placeholder handle
after converting it into a reparse point.

Example (export a fresh /export as a writable test share):

  1. Server:
     printf 'target\n' > /export/file
     mkdir /export/subdir
     printf 'nested\n' > /export/subdir/file
  2. Client, with SMB3 POSIX extensions enabled on the server:
     for mode in noposix posix; do
         mount -t cifs //${server_ip}/test /mnt \
             -o username=${smb_user},vers=3.1.1,$mode || exit 1
         ln -s file /mnt/remote-$mode
         ln -s subdir /mnt/remote-dir-$mode
         ln -s missing /mnt/remote-dangling-$mode
         readlink /mnt/remote-$mode
         cat /mnt/remote-$mode
         cat /mnt/remote-dir-$mode/file
         readlink /mnt/remote-dangling-$mode
         mv /mnt/remote-$mode /mnt/renamed-$mode
         readlink /mnt/renamed-$mode
         rm /mnt/renamed-$mode
         test -f /mnt/file
         umount /mnt || exit 1
     done

Expect file, target, nested, missing and file from each pass. Remount
each mode and read the directory and dangling links created in the
other mode. On the server, getfattr shows user.ksmbd.symlink on these
placeholders; they are not native Unix symlinks locally.

Direct SMB tests must also reject WRITE, EOF/allocation changes and
zeroing through the original handle after SET, including after a normal
FileBasicInformation update. Native links from earlier stages must
remain readable. Non-POSIX absolute targets remain unsupported.

The empty-directory and public-EA prechecks are not serialized against
concurrent local modifications; this stage does not promise an atomic
conversion under such mutations.

Code and test instructions generated with OpenAI Codex assistance.
